  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If tangents are drawn to the ellipse $x^{2}+2 y^{2}=2$ at all\r\n\r\npoints on the ellipse other than its four vertices then the mid points of the tangents intercepted between the coordinate axes lie on the curve :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "BeS6K",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4 x^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2 y^{2}}=1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "x8ZuJ",
      "text": "$\\frac{x^{2}}{4}+\\frac{y^{2}}{2}=1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TxsMk",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2 x^{2}}+\\frac{1}{4 y^{2}}=1$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "A45sg",
      "text": "$\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+\\frac{y^{2}}{4}=1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given the equation of ellipse,\r\n\r\n$\\frac{x^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+y^{2}=1$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/vmgJttUChProNB4hclfuKAWV81BNlw8ZEqtF3ICVk3Q.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\cos \\theta x}{2}+y \\sin \\theta=1$\r\n\r\n$P\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\cos \\theta}, 0\\right)$ and $Q\\left(0, \\frac{1}{\\sin \\theta}\\right)$\r\n\r\nLet mid point be $(h, k)$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow h=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2} \\cos \\theta}, k=\\frac{1}{2 \\sin \\theta}$\r\n\r\nAs $\\cos ^{2} \\theta+\\sin ^{2} \\theta=1$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\frac{1}{2 h^{2}}+\\frac{1}{4 k^{2}}=1$\r\n\r\nLocus is $\\frac{1}{2 x^{2}}+\\frac{1}{4 y^{2}}=1$",
    "image": null
  },
